Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 01:17:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] C7 GMAT: step to each node by its TDB epoch, not by elapsed
 time

The gmat job's second run (Flight dynamics run 42534549174, at bec4ae298) halted on the SPK leg's
last step, 3.2e-9 day (about 0.28 ms) past the kernel's coverage: GMAT counts elapsed time in A.1
seconds, the kernel's nodes are TDB, and over the file's 30 days the TDB-TT periodic term moves the
two about 0.28 ms apart. Both scripts now stop each step at the next node's TDB modified Julian date
(t = mjd0 + k * 600 / 86400, a TDBModJulian stop condition). The comparison and its bar are
unchanged. RESULTS (C7) records the run.
